review.objective:
Replace per-query full-file scanning with a deterministic, indexed, two-stage retrieval system that:

1. selects candidates without reopening every source file;
2. ranks task-specific files/symbols/tests/dependencies using discriminative signals;
3. expands only the most useful exact source spans;
4. fits the serialized pack to an explicit token budget;
5. abstains or asks for broader context when fidelity is insufficient;
6. keeps all omitted information locally retrievable through stable handles.

review.inputs_outputs_contracts:
ContextSnapshot deve conter no mínimo:

- schema_version, snapshot_id, repository_id e revision;
- root_hash, build config hash e producer version;
- source set, exclusions e reason codes;
- graph handles por escala: micro (símbolos/spans), meso (módulos/fluxos) e macro (subsistemas/ADRs);
- content hash por nó e aresta, causal/dependency links e freshness;
- task query, selection policy, budget e omissions;
- confidence calibrada, fidelity result e evidência do gate;
- handles reversíveis para expandir qualquer resumo até a fonte.

